+    of the evals folder)'
+  basis: 'Principle G4 (harness-standard.md lines 95-102): a decision names its source; an answer with no source
+    cannot be checked. Principle G6 (ADR 049 lines 53 and 59; ADR 057 line 75): no skill reads the evals folder,
+    so the file names are all the skill has. no-unbacked-recommendation rule (project memory ''never recommend when
+    you do not know'').'
+  problem: ADR 057 says an eval file is named by its feature id and covers that feature's failure conditions. From
+    a file name the skill can know that a scenario file exists for a feature. It cannot know that the scenario 'says
+    the builder fixes it'. The example teaches the skill to write that claim, and it is shown to the person as a
+    fact in the brief. The out_of_date records are also never checked against the file list (edit_slice.py reads
+    no out_of_date).
+  leads_to: The brief can state something about an eval that is false, or name a file that does not exist, and the
+    person cannot tell. The reason on that line has no source.
+  fix: 'Write the out_of_date reason from what is known: ''the eval for feature X may test this line; check it after
+    the edit''. Have check-list refuse an out_of_date record that is not in edit-evals.txt or in the epics of edit-before.json.'
